is incredibly moving, thrilling, and important story about an American hero who deserves to be remembered, and admired.” —Candice Millard, author of Hero of the Empire Facing death rather than enslavement—a story of one man's triumphant choice and ultimate rise to national hero It was a mild May morning in Charleston, South Carolina, in 1862, the second year of the Civil War, when a twenty-three-year-old slave named Robert Smalls did the unthinkable and boldly seized a Confederate steamer. With his wife and two young children hidden on board, Smalls and a small crew ran a gauntlet of heavily armed fortifications in Charleston Harbor and delivered the valuable vessel and the massive guns it carried to nearby Union forces. To be unsuccessful was a death sentence for all.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"History","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-be-free-or-die-the-amazing-story-of-robert-smalls-escape-from-slavery-to-union-hero-cate-lineber"}],"displaySummary":"With his wife and two young children hidden on board, Smalls and a small crew ran a gauntlet of heavily armed fortifications in Charleston Harbor and delivered the valuable vessel and the massive guns it carried to nearby Union forces. To be unsuccessful was a death sentence for all.","primarySubject":"History","primaryTopic":"American Civil War","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"History","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"History","score":3,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"History","mappedSubject":"History","score":3,"confidence":"medium","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-be-free-or-die-the-amazing-story-of-robert-smalls-escape-from-slavery-to-union-hero-cate-lineber","id":"subject-evidence-book-be-free-or-die-the-amazing-story-of-robert-smalls-escape-from-slavery-to-union-hero-cate-lineber-1"},{"source":"award_category","rawLabel":"G